        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Menelik II</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1844 CE – 1913 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">19 August 1844 (or 17 August) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankober">Ankober</a>, Shewa, as Sahle Maryam; son of Haile Melekot, Negus of Shewa, and Ejigayehu; of the Shewan branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomonic-dynasty">Solomonic dynasty</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">12 December 1913 (also placed in the night of 12 to 13 December), after strokes from 1906; buried in a mausoleum at the Menelik Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">King (Negus) of Shewa from 1866 to 1889, quasi-independent from 1878; Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1889 until his death in 1913</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Battle of Adwa</a> in 1896; the southern conquests that took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> to its greatest extent; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wuchale">Treaty of Wuchale</a> and its two versions; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djibouti">Djibouti</a> railway; a cabinet of ministers, schools and a state bank; the atrocities and enslavement associated with the annexations</span></div>
        </div>
